   "name": "Balancing by inspection",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A balanced equation has the same number of each kind of atom on both sides. This obeys the law of conservation of mass. Change only the coefficients, never the subscripts. Inspection is trial and error: N₂ + H₂ → NH₃ becomes N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃."
    }
   },
